# Auto commit & push

The user has granted standing permission: after completing meaningful code changes in this project, **commit and push to GitHub** without waiting for them to ask each time.

## When to commit & push
- After finishing a user-requested feature, fix, or deploy-relevant change
- Include related files in one commit when they belong to the same change
- Skip trivial-only edits (typo in chat reply with no file changes)

## How
1. `git status`, `git diff`, `git log -5 --oneline` in parallel
2. Stage relevant files (never `.env`, credentials, secrets, `node_modules`)
3. Commit with a concise message focused on why
4. `git push -u origin HEAD` (or the tracked remote/branch) — **push is allowed**
5. Report the commit hash and that push succeeded (or the error)

## Safety
- Never `git push --force` to main/master unless the user explicitly asks in that message
- Never update git config
- Never skip hooks unless explicitly asked
- If there is no git remote yet, say so and ask for the GitHub repo URL once
